Include <strings.h> for strcasecmp

`Bones.c` includes `<string.h>` with the comment "strcasecmp", which is true on macOS and on
glibc and is not POSIX: `strcasecmp` is declared in `<strings.h>`, and FreeBSD's `<string.h>`
does not pull that in. This target is FreeBSD-derived, so the call arrives undeclared and the
file is the only one of Bugdom's 78 C sources that does not compile.

Adding the include rather than declaring `strcasecmp` in our own `<string.h>`: that header is
the SDK's freestanding libc and it should say what the platform says, not what the two systems
upstream happens to build on say.
---
diff --git a/src/Skeleton/Bones.c b/src/Skeleton/Bones.c
index 2ced97b..db1ab7d 100644
--- a/src/Skeleton/Bones.c
+++ b/src/Skeleton/Bones.c
@@ -11,7 +11,8 @@
 
 #include "game.h"
 
-#include <string.h>				// strcasecmp
+#include <string.h>
+#include <strings.h>			// strcasecmp
 
 
 /****************************/
